course: dictionary
lesson: 12115
title: Everyday words
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words belong to everyday talk, and some belong to careful writing. Colloquially means in everyday, informal speech. «A television is colloquially called a telly» tells you that people often say telly when they chat, even though the full word is television.
explain: Writers choose words to suit the place. In a school report or a letter to the head teacher, you write television. With your friends, you might say telly. Both words are correct; they just fit different places.
explain: Look for clues. Words like loo, arvo or telly are usually marked informal or slang in a dictionary. The phrase «colloquially known as» introduces the everyday name for something, so read on to find the more formal word too.
fact: Colloquially means in everyday, informal speech, not in formal writing.
fact: Colloquial is the adjective, and colloquially is the adverb that tells you how something is said.
fact: «A television is colloquially called a telly.»
fact: «Loo» is a colloquial word for toilet, and «arvo» is a colloquial word for afternoon in Australia.
fact: A dictionary may mark colloquial words as informal or slang, so check the label when you are unsure.
exercise: Which word is used colloquially for television? | monitor | television | broadcasting | *telly
exercise: «Dad says he is going to watch the telly tonight.» In this sentence, telly is used in which kind of speech? | Formal writing | Maths problems | *Everyday, informal speech | Scientific reports
exercise: Which sentence is written in colloquial, everyday speech? | "The committee shall convene at noon." | "Pursuant to the agreement, payment is due." | "The meeting is hereby adjourned." | *"Hey, want to grab a bite to eat?"
test: In Australia, which word is used colloquially for afternoon? | *Arvo | Noon | Dusk | Morning
test: «Loo» is colloquially used for which place? | Kitchen | Bedroom | *Toilet | Garden
exam: Which sentence uses colloquially correctly? | *"Mum says the big machine is colloquially called the washer, but its proper name is washing machine." | "The colloquially is a long, formal document." | "The class went colloquially to the museum on Friday." | "Colloquially, the sun sets in the north every day."
